# Slim serving-only dependency set for the concept-explorer web deployment.
#
# This is the single source of truth for the *deployed* environment. It is
# intentionally separate from pyproject.toml / uv.lock so the offline pipeline
# install (torch, docling, agentic-mbse, sysml-codegen, local path deps) stays
# untouched (FR-3). See .project/completed/20260821_explorer-web-hosting/{spec,design}.md.
#
# Compile to a fully-pinned lockfile (direct + transitive) with:
#   uv pip compile requirements-serve.in -o requirements-serve.txt --prerelease=explicit
# (--prerelease=explicit confines any pre-release allowance to packages pinned to
#  one explicitly, so numpy/scipy/pydantic stay on stable releases. 1costingfe is
#  pinned to a public GitHub tag now, so the flag is a no-op, but keep it so a
#  future alpha bump of 1costingfe doesn't drag transitive deps onto pre-releases.)
# Commit both files. Regenerate on any bump (e.g. a new 1costingfe tag).
#
# 1costingfe is pinned to the public GitHub tag v0.1.1 (1cFE/1costingfe), NOT a
# PyPI release. We install from the tag's source tarball (codeload archive URL)
# rather than git+https, so the slim Docker image needs no git binary — pip
# fetches and builds it directly. The v0.1.1 build makes JAX OPTIONAL: numpy is
# the base dependency and jax/jaxlib are an opt-in [jax] extra. We install WITHOUT
# the extra, so the served image carries no jax/jaxlib (forward()/sensitivity()
# run on numpy; the library auto-detects the backend). This drops jax+jaxlib+scipy
# from the deploy, which is what fixes the Railway out-of-memory (the jaxlib RSS +
# per-request tracing was tipping the container over its limit).
#
# NOTE: 1costingfe still gates off the 0D physics solvers by default; the
# explorer re-enables them at runtime (model_setup_helpers.py flips
# MODELS_0D_ENABLED / SIZING_FEATURES_ENABLED). This works because the v0.1.1
# build still SHIPS the solver modules (layers/{tokamak,mirror,physics}.py).
# If a future tag deletes them (not just gates), tokamak concepts
# (01/21/28/29/33) will 500 — re-verify the parity check on any bump.

1costingfe @ https://github.com/1cFE/1costingfe/archive/refs/tags/v0.1.1.tar.gz  # numpy-only build (no jax/jaxlib) → import costingfe for /api/compute
fastapi
uvicorn[standard]
